<title>UK: Morgan Stanley set calls on General Electric.</title>
<headline>Morgan Stanley set calls on General Electric.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank Morgan Stanley said it has issued issued 300,000 European-style capped call warrants, on General Electric Co.</p>
<p>One warrants control one share.</p>
<p> STRIKE PRICE 1  $0.01		   STRIKE PRICE 2 $63.0</p>
<p> ISSUE PRICE    *$59.20		  MAX RETURN   *22.48 PCT P/A</p>
<p>DISCOUNT REFERENCE PRICE  *8.53 PCT</p>
<p> EXPIRY	    15.DEC.97	     PAYDATE	28.AUG.97</p>
<p>SPOT REFERENCE  $64.723</p>
<p> NOTES	     IF THE SHARE PRICE AT EXPIRATION IS AT OR ABOVE</p>
<p>		     STRIKE 2 (CAP) CASH PAYMENT OF $63.0</p>
<p>		     IF THE SHARE PRICE IS BELOW THE STRIKE 2</p>
<p>		     PHYSICAL DELIVERY OF ON GENERAL ELECTRIC CO.</p>
<p>		     COMMON SHARE.</p>
<p>*INDICATIVE</p>
<p>BANK MORGAN STANLEY TERM THE WARRANTS 'EROS' -ENHANCED RETURN</p>
<p>OR SECURITY.</p>
<p>--Reuter London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
